course: dictionary
lesson: 1067
title: One word, many jobs: bounce
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bounce changes its job depending on the words around it. Read the clues. «The ball bounced off the wall and landed at my feet.» Here bounce means to hit a surface and spring back.
explain: «The children bounced on the trampoline all afternoon.» Bounce means to jump up and down again and again. The trampoline is the clue. Bounce can also be a noun, as in «The ball had a good bounce», which means its springy quality.
explain: Use the swap check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «The ball sprang back off the wall» works, so spring back is right.
fact: Bounce can be a verb or a noun: you can bounce a ball, or a ball can have a good bounce.
fact: «Bounce» means to hit a surface and spring back, like a ball on the floor.
fact: «Bounce» also means to jump up and down again and again, like on a trampoline.
fact: «Bounce back» is a phrase meaning to recover after a problem.
fact: An email bounces when it comes back because it could not be delivered.
exercise: «A bouncy ball bounces a little lower each time it hits the floor.» What does bounces mean here? | Rolls slowly away | Breaks into pieces | Falls asleep | *Springs back up off the floor
exercise: «The children bounced on the trampoline all afternoon.» What does bounced mean? | Sat very still | Sent an email that could not be delivered | Hit a wall and fell silent | *Jumped up and down again and again
exercise: Dad says, «Your email has bounced.» What does this mean? | It was sent twice by mistake | It was read by everyone who received it | *It came back because it could not be delivered | It jumped out of the computer
test: «Sifakas are lemurs built for leaping. On the ground they bounce sideways with their arms up, like dancers.» What does bounce suggest here? | Dig holes in the sand | *Hop or spring in a light, lively way | Fight with other animals | Sleep on their backs
test: «A red apple looks red because it bounces red light and soaks up the other colours.» What does bounces mean here? | Makes a loud noise | Drops the light on the floor | Turns the light off completely | *Sends back red light instead of soaking it up
exam: «She bounced back after the bad day.» What does bounced back mean? | Jumped off the bed in a hurry | Sent the day back to the start | *Recovered and felt better | Forgot the day completely
